1
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,560
I, Jiang Xiaobai, a legal advocate,

2
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:10,880
have an injustice to report.

3
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,600
By law,

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,360
anyone who appeals
directly to the Emperor

5
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,520
must cross a thirty-foot bed of nails

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,680
before being granted an audience.

7
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:22,080
I accept.

8
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,320
Open the palace gates.

9
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,200
(If I can seek justice for the people,)

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,080
(why should I fear death?)

11
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,200
(Even if it's the gates of hell,)

12
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,160
(I, Jiang Xiaobai,)

13
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:42,360
(will see it through to the end.)

14
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:06,460
=The Cruel Tribunal=
=Episode 1=

15
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,480
Where am I?

16
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,160
Am I dreaming?

17
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:42,520
(What are they doing?)

18
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:46,080
(Is this a reality show?)

19
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,880
(What network is this?)

20
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:56,400
(These people)

21
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:58,920
(must all be extras, right?)

22
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:02,200
(How much do they get paid a day?)

23
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:28,520
I

24
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,120
have established the facts.

25
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,080
Yang Dou,

26
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:31,840
you,

27
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,560
as

28
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:34,480
the owner of the transport vessel,

29
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:35,600
were responsible

30
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:36,920
for ensuring your client,

31
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,640
Wang Er, had his goods

32
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,080
delivered safely.

33
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:41,960
But you acted on your own

34
00:03:42,280 --> 00:03:43,960
and threw the goods into the river,

35
00:03:44,040 --> 00:03:45,360
failing to fulfill your duty.

36
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:46,400
I've been wronged!

37
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,320
I only did it to save lives, Your Honor!

38
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,360
And you still refuse
to admit you were wrong?

39
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:53,640
Advocate Jiang,

40
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,080
say something!

41
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,240
Wait.

42
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:58,440
Is she

43
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,440
the advocate you hired?

44
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,560
You asked a woman to defend you?

45
00:04:04,320 --> 00:04:04,840
You there,

46
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,560
go outside.

47
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:08,840
Hold this for me.

48
00:04:12,880 --> 00:04:13,600
Official Huang,

49
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,280
I take issue with what you just said.

50
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,680
What law says women
can't defend a client?

51
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:19,120
Heaven and earth
draw no line between yin and yang.

52
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,490
Why should we draw one
between woman and man?

53
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:22,310
We're here today to argue
the merits of this case.

54
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,840
What does my gender have to do with it?

55
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,240
Look at the words above your head.

56
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:29,700
(Bright Mirror Hangs High)

57
00:04:29,700 --> 00:04:30,660
(Rise to Great Success)

58
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,320
Mr. Wang Er.

59
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,440
How many years have you worked on boats?

60
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:35,550
I've never worked on a boat.

61
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:35,840
But...

62
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:36,680
But I've been on one.

63
00:04:36,680 --> 00:04:38,760
When the storm hit,
did water get into the boat?

64
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:39,240
Yes.

65
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:41,240
But that didn't mean
the boat was going to sink.

66
00:04:41,360 --> 00:04:43,560
What did you base that judgment on?

67
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:44,080
Base it on?

68
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,320
My basis...

69
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,500
I just didn't think it would sink.

70
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,520
You thought?

71
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:49,790
Mr. Wang Er,
what do you do for a living?

72
00:04:49,800 --> 00:04:50,560
I'm a

73
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,480
merchant.

74
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:52,440
Mr. Wang Er,

75
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,920
if your house caught fire right now,

76
00:04:53,930 --> 00:04:55,200
would you hurry
out of the burning house,

77
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,870
or go back inside
to gather your belongings?

78
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:58,280
I'd run out first, of course.

79
00:04:58,310 --> 00:04:58,890
Then the fire...

80
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,120
Mr. Yang Dou,

81
00:05:02,500 --> 00:05:04,070
how many years
have you been a boat captain?

82
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:05,900
I've worked on boats
with my father since I was a child.

83
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:06,400
To this day,

84
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:07,520
it's been over thirty years.

85
00:05:07,530 --> 00:05:08,990
How many people
were aboard the cargo boat that day?

86
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:09,400
There were

87
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,120
the oarsman,

88
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:10,800
the escort,

89
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,400
and me.

90
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,080
Three of us in total.

91
00:05:12,120 --> 00:05:13,070
What day did the incident occur?

92
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:13,640
Yesterday.

93
00:05:14,680 --> 00:05:15,520
Official Huang,

94
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,240
what was the weather like yesterday?

95
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,200
Yesterday?

96
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:20,240
The weather was clear,

97
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:22,840
but a sudden,
strange gust did blow through.

98
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,880
Then the facts are quite clear.

99
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:25,960
As you said,

100
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,400
yesterday's storm did indeed occur.

101
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:28,920
While Yang Dou was transporting

102
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,480
his client Wang Er's goods,

103
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,760
he encountered a dangerous storm.

104
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:33,880
Based on his thirty years
of sailing experience,

105
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,120
he knew that in such a crisis,

106
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:36,000
if he didn't act immediately

107
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,520
and throw all the cargo

108
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:38,320
into the river,

109
00:05:38,400 --> 00:05:40,320
the boat would sink
and lives would be lost.

110
00:05:40,360 --> 00:05:42,080
Three lives were at stake.

111
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,160
Under those circumstances,

112
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,000
or rather,

113
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:46,680
Yang Dou was justified
in throwing the cargo overboard,

114
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,160
because

115
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,840
Mr. Wang Er also believes

116
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:50,680
that human life
matters more than property.

117
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:52,360
It was no easy decision for Yang Dou,

118
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,520
but he had no other choice.

119
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,280
I believe

120
00:05:54,280 --> 00:05:55,040
Yang Dou's actions

121
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,240
constitute necessity under modern law.

122
00:05:57,280 --> 00:05:58,760
Necessity?

123
00:05:58,770 --> 00:06:00,440
The legal interpretation
of necessity is as follows.

124
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:02,190
A person who meets the conditions
for necessity may be

125
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:04,080
partially or fully exempt
from civil liability.

126
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:04,800
Clearly,

127
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:06,840
the cargo was thrown overboard
because of a natural disaster,

128
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:09,000
and the danger
was immediate and imminent.

129
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,670
Throwing the cargo overboard
was the only option.

130
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:11,070
Therefore,

131
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:12,240
in that critical moment,

132
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:13,760
to save the three lives aboard,

133
00:06:13,770 --> 00:06:15,000
Yang Dou threw the cargo into the river.

134
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,360
It was the only right thing to do.

135
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:17,800
Yang Dou should not be punished.

136
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,600
Nor should he
be liable for Wang Er's losses.

137
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,200
If Yang Dou is punished today,

138
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,720
who would dare, in a future crisis,

139
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:23,600
to step forward

140
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:25,520
and save someone in mortal danger?

141
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:27,460
(Bright Mirror Hangs High.
Rise to Great Success)

142
00:06:29,040 --> 00:06:30,080
Excuse me.

143
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:31,040
Leave us.

144
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:36,740
(Nothing)

145
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:37,390
What do you think

146
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,440
of this case?

147
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:40,440
That young woman

148
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,920
is truly extraordinary.

149
00:06:42,160 --> 00:06:44,680
Her manner of speaking
may seem a little strange,

150
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:45,640
but

151
00:06:45,760 --> 00:06:46,920
her reasoning is sound,

152
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:48,280
and her arguments are convincing.

153
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:51,000
The people see you as a good official.

154
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,920
If those who save lives
are treated justly,

155
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:55,160
the people will surely

156
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,680
look up to you.

157
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,500
(Bright Mirror Hangs High)

158
00:07:00,520 --> 00:07:01,720
Defendant Yang Dou,

159
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:03,350
although your act
of discarding the cargo

160
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:04,520
was improper,

161
00:07:04,760 --> 00:07:05,040
your

162
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:05,880
intention

163
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,240
was to save

164
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,040
the lives of the three people aboard.

165
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:10,480
When faced

166
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:11,880
with two evils,

167
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,080
one must choose the lesser.

168
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:15,320
Your intentions were commendable.

169
00:07:15,480 --> 00:07:16,240
I hereby rule that

170
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:17,720
the defendant, Yang Dou,

171
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:19,520
shall bear no criminal responsibility

172
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,880
and need not compensate

173
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:22,560
Wang Er for his losses.

174
00:07:22,880 --> 00:07:23,640
But...

175
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:25,160
This case is now closed.

176
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:27,000
Let there be no further dispute.

177
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:30,000
Court dismissed.

178
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:31,190
Thank you for your
wise judgment, Your Honor.

179
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:32,510
Thank you for your
wise judgment, Your Honor.

180
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,120
Advocate Jiang,

181
00:07:33,400 --> 00:07:34,520
thank you so much.

182
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:36,040
You're my savior.

183
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,630
You did nothing wrong
in the first place.

184
00:07:37,640 --> 00:07:39,190
A little case like this
was a piece of cake.

185
00:07:40,890 --> 00:07:41,600
A piece of cake?

186
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:42,800
I'm off. Bye.

187
00:07:43,080 --> 00:07:44,000
Advocate Jiang, wait!

188
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:45,560
Advocate Jiang,

189
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:47,200
thank you so much for today.

190
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:48,240
By the way,

191
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:49,200
what is this place?

192
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:49,880
This...

193
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,280
This is Bojue Kingdom.

194
00:07:51,440 --> 00:07:52,360
Bojue Kingdom?

195
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,320
Never heard of it.

196
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:55,520
You must be joking.

197
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,160
You're an advocate here
in Bojue Kingdom.

198
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:58,760
How could you not know where you are?

199
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:00,360
I'm really an advocate?

200
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,560
Of course you are.

201
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:02,560
Well,

202
00:08:02,640 --> 00:08:03,600
I'll be going then.

203
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,240
Bojue Kingdom.

204
00:08:11,840 --> 00:08:13,040
An advocate.

205
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:17,240
Did I travel back in time?

206
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,920
Dear heavens,

207
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,880
you couldn't bear to see me
slave away anymore,

208
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:23,800
so you brought me here

209
00:08:23,800 --> 00:08:24,760
to let me change my fate

210
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:26,640
and start a glorious new life.

211
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:31,540
(Blessing the People)

212
00:08:32,920 --> 00:08:34,410
Pastries!

213
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:36,800
I need to survive before I can thrive.

214
00:08:37,020 --> 00:08:41,500
(Recruitment Notice:
This jade shop seeks one assistant)

215
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,980
(Applicants must
be articulate and well read)

216
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,160
(Shop assistant wanted.)

217
00:08:46,680 --> 00:08:49,520
(Must be articulate.)

218
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,680
(That's describing me perfectly!)

219
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,200
(Here's my chance to make some money.)

220
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,000
(Treasure House)

221
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:57,800
Boss.

222
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,560
Looking for something?

223
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:03,280
Boss, I'm here about the job.

224
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,080
What can you do?

225
00:09:06,280 --> 00:09:07,680
I can do anything.

226
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:08,440
You...

227
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,680
I can wipe tables and mop floors.

228
00:09:11,160 --> 00:09:12,280
I know antiques too.

229
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,200
Step aside.

230
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,200
I've got a customer.

231
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,120
Young Master,

232
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,400
looking for anything?

233
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Just browsing.

234
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:22,520
Anything you'd recommend?

235
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:25,480
Well, you've come
at just the right time.

236
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,280
I just acquired a real treasure.

237
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:28,440
Let me show you.

238
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:42,360
Take a look.

239
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,640
I bought this treasure
from Pugan Kingdom

240
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:53,880
in the southwest for fifty gold pieces.

241
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:55,960
Why did you smash it?

242
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:56,800
I don't care.

243
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,160
You have to pay me back.

244
00:09:58,440 --> 00:09:59,960
You deliberately let go

245
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:00,990
when you handed it to me.

246
00:10:01,360 --> 00:10:02,160
Who saw that?

247
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,360
Who saw it?

248
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:05,080
You're not leaving.

249
00:10:05,320 --> 00:10:06,560
I saw it.

250
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,720
You deliberately threw the bracelet

251
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,480
onto the floor.

252
00:10:11,600 --> 00:10:13,240
As the saying goes,
never take your eyes off gold,

253
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,460
and never pass jade hand to hand.

254
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,320
You run an antique and jade shop.

255
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,680
Surely you know that.

256
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,520
You obviously set him up on purpose.

257
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:20,560
Enough nonsense.

258
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:21,760
I'm telling you,

259
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:24,480
you break it, you pay for it.

260
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,680
Otherwise,

261
00:10:25,880 --> 00:10:27,200
let's see if either of you

262
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:28,500
can make it out that door today.

263
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:29,880
Men!

264
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,000
Run, you idiot!

265
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:31,540
After them!

266
00:10:31,540 --> 00:10:31,960
Hurry!

267
00:10:34,130 --> 00:10:35,040
Don't run!

268
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,840
- Stop!
- Stop!

269
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:38,600
Stop!

270
00:10:43,240 --> 00:10:43,920
Don't run!

271
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:46,880
Split up!

272
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:47,800
Until we meet again!

273
00:10:50,370 --> 00:10:51,680
Come on, split up and chase them!

274
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:52,640
Follow me!

275
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:01,000
Dear heavens,

276
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,440
did you bring me here
to build a glorious new life,

277
00:11:03,440 --> 00:11:05,160
or to put me through hell?

278
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:12,480
Free porridge!

279
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,560
Easy now.

280
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:15,240
Come on, line up.

281
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,160
Here you go.

282
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:20,900
Take it easy.

283
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:21,800
Come back if you need more.

284
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:22,240
Thank you.

285
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,000
Next.

286
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,800
Come on, there's no need to rush.

287
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,120
There's enough for everyone.

288
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:28,680
Isn't that the lady advocate?

289
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:29,960
Yes, that's her.

290
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,440
Line up over here.

291
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:31,800
Thank you.

292
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:32,760
Come back if you need more.

293
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:33,680
Miss.

294
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,600
Come.

295
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,400
Do we know each other?

296
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:39,920
I know you.

297
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,840
We've only just met.

298
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:43,760
Why are you treating me to a meal?

299
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:46,080
I just wanted to be friends with you.

300
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,120
Friends?

301
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,160
Don't you have any friends?

302
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:50,960
Why make friends
with a complete stranger like me?

303
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,560
I don't have any friends.

304
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:54,640
My parents died when I was young,

305
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,760
so my uncle raised me.

306
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:59,640
He's always been very strict with me,

307
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:01,400
so I rarely get to go out.

308
00:12:01,720 --> 00:12:03,440
I've never had the chance
to make friends.

309
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:05,840
Your uncle is way out of line.

310
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,400
What right does he have
to stop you from making friends?

311
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,240
Tell me who he is.

312
00:12:08,240 --> 00:12:09,640
I'll challenge him myself.

313
00:12:10,920 --> 00:12:12,120
He's Prince Luan.

314
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,600
A prince?

315
00:12:18,120 --> 00:12:19,920
Then there's no need
to bother His Highness.

316
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:21,600
(Dear heavens,)

317
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:23,440
(you've really come through for me.)

318
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,600
(I've barely arrived, and you've
already sent me someone important.)

319
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:27,240
(My chance to live in wealth and luxury)

320
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,720
(has finally arrived.)

321
00:12:46,770 --> 00:12:47,840
Why has the sedan stopped?

322
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:18,750
♪The candle burns down
to its final glow♪

323
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:22,100
♪Cold fragrance clings to my hem♪

324
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:24,500
♪You gently smooth my hair♪

325
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:27,420
♪Yet your gaze drifts far away♪

326
00:13:29,870 --> 00:13:32,290
♪A hidden blade lies beneath your smile♪

327
00:13:32,660 --> 00:13:35,970
♪You turn away
as if nothing has changed♪

328
00:13:36,580 --> 00:13:38,140
♪Step by step, I walk away♪

329
00:13:38,310 --> 00:13:41,640
♪Each step breaks my heart anew♪

330
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:47,250
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

331
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:50,860
♪Why leave me
standing alone in the wind?♪

332
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:53,920
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

333
00:13:53,920 --> 00:13:57,950
♪Yet all that's left
is warmth upon my fingertips♪

334
00:13:58,190 --> 00:14:01,240
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

335
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:04,290
♪And write of every meeting
and every parting♪

336
00:14:04,290 --> 00:14:07,040
♪If next life asks
about the days gone by♪

337
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:10,260
♪I'll only say that once♪

338
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:12,500
♪I called your name♪

339
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:19,330
♪The silent stars hang low♪

340
00:14:20,750 --> 00:14:22,960
♪The river keeps flowing east♪

341
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:26,090
♪I linger in the old tower♪

342
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:29,870
♪Waiting for you,
though all is now empty♪

343
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,640
♪This life still owes us a bow♪

344
00:14:34,520 --> 00:14:37,300
♪May the next repay us with a dream♪

345
00:14:38,070 --> 00:14:40,310
♪Beyond here lie
endless mountains and rivers♪

346
00:14:40,310 --> 00:14:46,550
♪I dare not turn for one last look♪

347
00:14:46,810 --> 00:14:49,690
♪If fate had not gone astray♪

348
00:14:50,290 --> 00:14:53,790
♪Why bury this heart beneath the frost?♪

349
00:14:53,790 --> 00:14:56,430
♪We shared one fleeting life together♪

350
00:14:56,430 --> 00:15:00,720
♪Now only fading warmth
remains in my palm♪

351
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:03,630
♪I'd melt this night into ink♪

352
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:06,780
♪And paint a winter between your brows♪

353
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,450
♪If we meet again in another life♪

354
00:15:09,770 --> 00:15:12,500
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

355
00:15:13,190 --> 00:15:15,480
♪Was when we first met?♪

356
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:19,140
♪Will you believe that tonight♪

357
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:22,030
♪Was when we met for the last time?♪
